WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.322
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:05.506
- People ask me that
question all the time:

00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:07.773
what is it feels like to get hit?

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.561
It's like a little explosion in your body,

00:00:09.561 --> 00:00:11.707
if they hit you at the right spot.

00:00:11.707 --> 00:00:14.883
But I'm not really trying to hurt them.

00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:17.406
Actually, except when
I'm hitting the body,

00:00:17.406 --> 00:00:20.949
I really like hearing people, like, grunt.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:23.949
(suspenseful music)

00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:28.571
There are very few female boxers that

00:00:29.741 --> 00:00:33.366
are still in the game
that have that longevity

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.816
in the sport that I've had.

00:00:35.816 --> 00:00:38.278
In 20 years of boxing, I've
never been knocked out,

00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:41.965
much less knocked down and
I think the reason for that

00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:44.767
is not just because I'm strong,

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.827
it's because I don't take punches.

00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:48.939
I'm never there to get punched.

00:00:48.939 --> 00:00:49.772
It's weird.

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:51.887
It's very hard for me to associate being

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:53.750
World Champion with my name.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.163
I mean, I have an office that has my belt

00:00:56.163 --> 00:01:00.772
and all these photos of all the
different titles that I've won,

00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:05.103
but I just don't feel
like it applies to me.

00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:07.593
(calm piano music)

00:01:07.593 --> 00:01:10.843
I was dancer so only when I was injured

00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:15.300
and knew that I couldn't dance anymore

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.145
that I took up something
else, just for exercise.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.607
So went into kickboxing

00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:23.688
and eventually into boxing.

00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:25.447
Because I started out as a dancer,

00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:28.438
one of the biggest elements that I bring

00:01:28.438 --> 00:01:30.688
into my boxing is movement.

00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:37.383
When I first came into boxing,
there were very few women

00:01:38.242 --> 00:01:41.697
and the mentality of
the guys that were here

00:01:41.697 --> 00:01:43.536
were that, "You shouldn't box."

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.800
"You're too pretty to box."

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.176
You know, ”Go back to dance or something else."

00:01:48.176 --> 00:01:51.307
This is a sport like any other sport.

00:01:51.307 --> 00:01:52.795
I can do it.

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:54.545
Any female can do it.

00:01:56.143 --> 00:02:00.226
The best recognition I
had was when someone said,

00:02:01.647 --> 00:02:06.581
"She fights like Pernell
Whitaker or Muhammad Ali."

00:02:06.581 --> 00:02:09.454
They didn't say I fought like a female.

00:02:09.454 --> 00:02:11.871
I'm 48 and for my next fight,

00:02:13.019 --> 00:02:17.186
I'm gonna try to be the
oldest female title holder

00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:21.350
and that would be in the
Guinness World Record,

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.705
so there's different
things that I need to win.

00:02:23.705 --> 00:02:25.640
There's different things that I need to do

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.884
and World Champion is just one of it.

00:02:27.884 --> 00:02:31.134
(upbeat melodic music)

